camss: switchable sensor links, for two cameras on one CSIPHY

THE PROBLEM
-----------
This phone has FIVE cameras and the SoC has FOUR CSI inputs, so two pairs share
an input through a MIPI switch: the front one with the wide angle, and the depth
one with the macro. In real use one is used at a time and switched over, which is
exactly what the switch exists for.

The device tree already allows it: camss_parse_ports() walks ALL endpoints with
fwnode_graph_for_each_endpoint(), and the CSIPHY is chosen by PORT number
-csd->interface.csiphy_id = vep.base.port-, not by endpoint. So two sensors on
the same port@1 both get registered and both go to CSIPHY1.

But then NEITHER of them captures:

    v4l2_subdev_link_validate_default: width does not match (source 2592, sink 4208)
    link was "s5k3t2 13-0010":0 -> "msm_csiphy1":0
    Failed to start media pipeline: -32

Because camss_subdev_notifier_complete() creates EVERY sensor -> csiphy link with

    MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE | MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED

With a single sensor per CSIPHY that makes no difference. With two, both links
stay enabled FOREVER -immutable means not even media-ctl can turn them off- and
when starting either one, validation also walks the other one's link, whose
format does not match. Both fail.

THE FIX
-------
Do not mark the link as immutable, and enable it only if it is the FIRST one on
that CSIPHY. That way:

  - with a single sensor, the link is still created enabled and nothing changes;
  - with two, the first stays enabled and the second disabled, and they are
    switched from user space:

        media-ctl -l '"s5k3t2 13-0010":0->"msm_csiphy1":0[0]'
        media-ctl -l '"hi1337 14-0021":0->"msm_csiphy1":0[1]'

    The MIPI switch does not have to be touched by hand: each sensor's driver
    puts it in its position when powering on and releases it when powering off.

WHY THIS IS NOT A HACK FOR THIS PHONE
-------------------------------------
Sharing a CSIPHY between two sensors with a switch is common in phones with more
cameras than inputs. Having the links be immutable makes it impossible by
construction, and there is no reason for them to be: immutable is for what
physically cannot be disconnected, and here it can.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -5170,6 +5170,28 @@
 	return 0;
 }

+/*
+ * camss_first_sensor_of_csiphy - whether this CSIPHY does not yet have any
+ * sensor enlazado
+ *
+ * On phones with more cameras than CSI inputs, two sensors share a CSIPHY
+ * through a MIPI switch. Only the first one is left enabled; the second one is
+ * created disabled and is switched from userspace. If both were left
+ * enabled, pipeline validation would walk both and would not capture
+ * ninguno.
+ */
+static bool camss_first_sensor_of_csiphy(struct media_entity *csiphy)
+{
+	struct media_pad *sink = &csiphy->pads[MSM_CSIPHY_PAD_SINK];
+	struct media_link *link;
+
+	list_for_each_entry(link, &csiphy->links, list)
+		if (link->sink == sink)
+			return false;
+
+	return true;
+}
+
 static int camss_subdev_notifier_complete(struct v4l2_async_notifier *async)
 {
 	struct camss *camss = container_of(async, struct camss, notifier);
@@ -5203,9 +5226,15 @@
 			return -EINVAL;
 		}

+		/*
+		 * NEITHER immutable NOR enabled if there is already another sensor on this CSIPHY.
+		 * An immutable link cannot be disabled, and with two sensors on
+		 * the same input that leaves both cameras unusable.
+		 */
 		ret = media_create_pad_link(sensor, i, input,
 					    MSM_CSIPHY_PAD_SINK,
-					    MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE | MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED);
+					    camss_first_sensor_of_csiphy(input) ?
+					    MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED : 0);
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			camss_link_err(camss, sensor->name, input->name, ret);
 			return ret;
